  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader, I want to save topics for reading without network, list them and remove them, so that I can read where there is no connection.\n\n### Scope\n\nAn HFRStorage store of saved topics and pages: save, list, load and evict. Device-only and excluded from backup (ADR 0013). It reuses the LOT-066 cache directory, evictor and budget. The spec decides and justifies what is saved (parsed `TopicPage` models or raw HTML), the on-disk format and its version, the eviction policy, and what happens to a page saved by an older build. Fetching the pages is the app's job (LOT-139, #229): HFRStorage imports neither HFRNetwork nor HFRParsing. Importing the legacy archive is LOT-067 (#92), not this lot.\n\n- Module: HFRStorage · Difficulty: medium · Priority: medium\n- Audit source: E-8 (`docs/audit/E-storage-vendors.md:339`; its \"out of scope\" remark is superseded by Q-5, \"in scope\", `docs/audit/README.md`), `OfflineStorage.m`\n- Legacy sources (read-only; francoisgn/hfrnow at `2440d79`, an ancestor of `origin/master`):\n  - `Classes/OfflineStorage.m:41-143` (set of offline topics keyed by post id; `NSKeyedArchiver` load and save), `:146-295` (page download into `<post>-<page>/index.html` under `Documents`, the last page fetched again, page limit `offline_max_pages`), `:336-437` (erase all, integrity check, read a saved page back) (at `2440d79`).\n  - `Classes/Topic.m:101-157` (archived topic fields) (at `2440d79`).\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-068-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-011 (#44, done)\n- LOT-066 (#91, done)\n\n### Blocked by\n\nnone: every dependency is merged.\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- None from HFR: the stored pages are existing topic captures (`R20`-`R28`, `RA1`-`RA5`) used as test inputs.\n- Legacy oracle: `tooling/legacy-oracle/samples/storage-offline.json` is a synthetic input; its legacy output is generated on the Mac by `run-oracle.sh` and not committed (LOT-004 spec). It matters for the LOT-067 importer only.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Save, list, load and evict the pages of a topic; a saved page loads back equal to what was saved (round trip on captured topic pages or their parsed models).\n- [ ] The format is versioned; a page saved by an older format version is migrated or dropped as the spec says, never a crash (tested).\n- [ ] Eviction goes through LOT-066's evictor and budget; the per-topic page limit (legacy `offline_max_pages`) and the last-page refresh rule are stated in the spec.\n- [ ] Device-only and excluded from backup (ADR 0013); per account or shared is decided in the spec.\n- [ ] No new public type in HFRModels without the core team's answer (`BLOCKED:` on this issue, core-model guard).\n- [ ] Swift Testing tests; `swift test` green on Linux and macOS CI; module rules of docs/ARCHITECTURE.md respected (`scripts/check-lot-deps.py` passes).\n- [ ] Spec `docs/lots/LOT-068-*.md` with legacy sources (file:line), edge cases and intentional differences; verified protocol facts in HFR-PROTOCOL §6c under this lot's own `###`.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).\n\n### Old issue (frozen)\n\n[francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR#89](https://github.com/francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR/issues/89) — read-only history.\n",
