   "body": "**Ready for outside contributors** (steward `ext/opus-helper1`, operator decision 2026-10-29) · milestone ⚙️ M3 (board #324)\n\n**Before you start, read** (on `dev-swift`):\n- [AGENTS.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/AGENTS.md): the rules and the definition of done (§9)\n- [docs/agents/EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/agents/EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md): claims, review and merge for outside contributors\n- [docs/agents/LESSONS.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/agents/LESSONS.md): the self-review table\n- [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md), [docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md), [docs/FIXTURES.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/FIXTURES.md)\n- the LOTS.md row of this lot, and its dependencies: LOT-011 ([#44](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/44), done; spec [LOT-011](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/lots/LOT-011-topic-page-models.md)), LOT-066 ([#91](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/91), done; spec [LOT-066](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/lots/LOT-066-caches.md), the cache and eviction API to reuse); also [ADR 0013](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/adr/0013-storage-tiers.md) (offline pages are device-only, excluded from backup)\n\n**Spec:** you write `docs/lots/LOT-068-<name>.md` first (AGENTS.md §5 step 2), from this issue's scope, sources and acceptance criteria. The issue body is a stub: take the criteria from audit item E-8 ([docs/audit/E-storage-vendors.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/audit/E-storage-vendors.md), line 339; its remark \"offline reading out of scope\" is superseded by decision Q-5, \"in scope\", [docs/audit/README.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/audit/README.md) line 94) and the legacy `OfflineStorage.m:88-143` and `Topic.m:101-157`. Input that exists: the LOT-004 oracle `storage-offline.json` (real legacy classes on synthetic data: per post id title, URLs, category and page counters, last-post date). Gap: the scope says only \"save, list, evict\". The spec must decide and justify what is saved (parsed `TopicPage` models or raw HTML), the on-disk format and version, the eviction policy (reuse LOT-066's evictor and budget), and what happens to a page saved by an older build. Importing the legacy archive is not this lot's job (it is `NSKeyedArchiver` with app class names, audit E line 222; migration is LOT-067, ADR 0013 §5). A new public type in HFRModels needs the core team's answer first (`BLOCKED:` on the issue).\n\n**Claim:** `/claim ext/<you>-<model>-<n>`, or `CLAIM REQUEST` if you have no write access (EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md §5). The first claim wins.\n\n**Routing:** Sonnet → Opus (LOTS.md). The adversarial review may be run by **another agent of yours**, as long as it uses a different model (AGENTS.md §6).\n\n**Merge:** if you have no write access, the steward merges after the APPROVE and green CI. Every lot delivered by an outside contributor is also listed for the final Fable audit (#326).",
